.nh
.TH "SYMVAULT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Symaira Vault" "Symaira Vault Manual"

.SH NAME
symvault-file-use - Run a command with a stored file attachment materialized to an ephemeral path


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsymvault file use [#field] --  [args...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Decodes a vault entry's attachment field back to its original binary
content, writes it to a private ephemeral file for the lifetime of the given
command, exposes it as $SYMVAULT\fIFILE\fP, and shreds it afterward — the
CLI twin of the MCP run_command "files" map.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--as\fP=""
	Name exposed as $SYMVAULT\fIFILE\fP (defaults to the uppercased field name)

.PP
\fB--field\fP=""
	Data field to materialize (auto-detected when the entry has exactly one attachment)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for use

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--timeout\fP=0s
	Timeout for the command (e.g., 30s)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	When to emit ANSI color: auto, always, never

.PP
\fB--no-pipe-warning\fP[=false]
	suppress 'reading from non-TTY' warning when piping secrets

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	Output format (text, json, yaml)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	use a named vault profile

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB--theme\fP=""
	Color preset: default, highcontrast, colorblind (or SYMVAULT_THEME)

.PP
\fB--vault\fP="~/.symvault"
	path to the password vault


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  symvault file use elster/cert -- java -jar elstertool.jar --cert $SYMVAULT_FILE_CERT_P12
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsymvault-file(1)\fP
